#ifdef GEO_BAKE_COVER
// The albedo bakes (geoAlbedo.ts): the shore bands' width as the land field's own variation over
// the texel (its four neighbours half a texel away), and only where the texel straddles the shore (the
// samples differ in sign): such a texel's sea, sand and shelf shares are what it covers. A texel wholly on
// land or at sea keeps the point's own bands (0): the distance-field width (fp × GR_LAND_M) is far too wide
// on the procedural shelves, and the variation alone paints every rough-ground texel near a coast sand.
float groundCoverBlur(vec3 n, float land, float fp){
  vec3 E, N; grTangent(n,E,N); float d=.5*fp/(GEO_R_KM*1000.);
